From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <barak+git@pearlmutter.net>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:27:16 +0100
Subject: refactor: share the rendering and saving code between GUI and batch

MainWindow and BatchCompare each had their own copy of the code that
highlights differences, renders and caches page pixmaps, and saves
differences as PDF (computeTextHighlights, addHighlighting,
computeVisualHighlights, paintOnImage, pixelRectForMargins,
pointRectForMargins, cacheKeys, populatePixmaps, paintSaveAs and
saveAsPdf, 73-100% identical), differing only in where the settings
came from: the GUI's widgets and QSettings, or fields in BatchCompare
that mirrored those widgets (zoomSpinBoxValue, marginsGroupBoxChecked,
...).  Fixes had to be made twice.

- renderer.{h,cpp}: RenderSettings holds everything that affects how
  differences are found and shown; DifferenceRenderer has the single
  copy of the code above (pixmaps(), paintPair(), saveAsPdf()); and
  loadPdf() opens a PDF with antialiasing, as both getPdf()s did, with
  the caller reporting errors in its own way.  The pixmap cache key now
  includes the highlighting settings too.
- MainWindow builds a RenderSettings from its widgets and settings
  (renderSettings()); BatchCompare keeps one (render) filled from its
  settings file, instead of the mirror fields.  CompareThreads stays
  outside RenderSettings, since it changes only how fast pages are
  compared, not the result.
- Dead code removed: MainWindow's unused CompareNotifier implementation
  and commented-out initCompareParams(), BatchCompare declarations of
  functions it never defined (showZones, showMargins, saveAsImages, ...),
  fields that were only ever assigned, and the unused file name
  parameters of the BatchCompare and CommandLineManager constructors.

About 800 lines fewer; the build is free of warnings with -Wall -Wextra.

Unchanged behaviour: all 29 tests pass, the offscreen GUI test behaves
as before, and with QT_HASH_SEED=0 disparPDFc gives the same results and
the same --pdfdiff pages (rasterized, below the timestamped header) as
before on 84 comparisons (7 file pairs, 3 modes, settings files with
margins and zoom, a composition mode, and other highlighting settings).
Without a fixed hash seed the highlighting varies from run to run, even
before this change; the next commit fixes that.

